# SOURCE OF TRUTH KEYWORDS: codeowners, release-security, signing, updater-pubkey, supply-chain
# WHAT:  Names the owner of every file that decides what ships to users or who can sign it.
# WHY:   The signing key and certificate live in repository secrets that any workflow running on
#        main or a tag can read, so a merged change to a workflow, the updater's public key or
#        endpoint, or the dependency lock files is a way to ship code or leak the keys. These paths
#        therefore ask for the owner's review by name. NOTE: GitHub only BLOCKS a merge on this
#        when branch protection requires code-owner review; until other people have write access
#        it is a review request, not a gate. Turn that rule on the day a collaborator is added.
# WHERE: Read by GitHub on every pull request.

